    <mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="Tube thief takedown"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Tube thief takedown
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What’s happening? </strong>Over the past 12 months, British Transport Police arrested around 462 suspects, many of them teenagers, in a major <a href="https://www.standard.co.uk/news/crime/btp-arrests-police-robbery-crackdown-london-train-tube-network-b1274469.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">crackdown on robberies</a> across London’s Tube and rail network. The operation targeted a surge in violent thefts affecting commuters at stations and on trains. Authorities aimed to deter repeat offenders, restore public confidence in the transport system, and prevent violence linked to knife crime.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Policing process:</strong> British Transport Police are policing the network through a mix of high-visibility patrols, covert operations, and technology-led enforcement. Plain-clothes officers operate on trains and platforms to identify and arrest suspects. Police are also using live facial recognition cameras during targeted operations to locate wanted individuals. Additional measures include knife-detection arches, search dogs, and rapid-response teams.  <br><br><strong>How to report incidents?</strong> Public can report robberies or suspicious activity on the rail and Tube network by texting 61016, which allows passengers to send details without drawing attention on a train or platform. If the situation is urgent or someone is in immediate danger, the public should dial 999.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" css-class="border-line" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
