  ">
    <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4g23npxpwgo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">An investigation has been launched after a technical glitch in the mobile banking apps of Lloyds Bank, Halifax and Bank of Scotland allowed some customers to see transactions belonging to other users</a>. Lloyds Banking Group apologised and said the problem was quickly identified and resolved, but regulators are currently reviewing the incident. It remains unclear how many customers were affected by the temporary data exposure.
  </td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
