  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly09j2542no" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Estée Lauder Companies sued British perfumer Jo Malone over the use of her name in a fragrance collaboration with retailer Zara.</a> The products were sold under Jo Loves, but the packaging used “A creation by Jo Malone CBE,” which Estée Lauder says breaches its trademark rights purchased in 1999. The company claims trademark infringement, breach of contract, and passing off, saying the branding could mislead customers into thinking the products are linked to Jo Malone London.
  </td>
</tr>
</mj-table>

