  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.espn.in/football/story/_/id/48182233/how-watch-uk-tv-channel-kick-live-stream" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Ryan Reynolds and Rob McElhenney will provide a special commentary broadcast when Wrexham AFC face Swansea City in the Championship at the Racecourse Ground</a>. The alternative coverage, titled Live From Wrexham with Rob &amp; Ryan, will air on Sky Sports alongside the standard broadcast. The show marks five years since the Hollywood pair bought the club and promises an unconventional commentary style.
  </td>
</tr>
</mj-table>
